# Line endings and binary handling, pinned for reproducibility.
#
# Why this file exists: the development box runs git with core.autocrlf=true, which means checkout
# line endings there depend on a local setting. Two things in this project are sensitive to that:
# rustfmt writes LF and reports a diff against a CRLF working copy, and the release manifest records
# SHA-256 over the exact bytes of each packaged file. A build that is only reproducible on machines
# with the same git config is not reproducible.
#
# Deliberately narrow. Only the sources whose formatter output is LF-normative, plus the artifacts
# that must never be text-converted at all. `.inf`, `.ps1`, `.toml` and the markdown docs are left
# alone on purpose: re-normalizing a file that a signed catalog has already hashed would turn a
# line-ending preference into a packaging change, and that trade is not worth making here.

*.rs text eol=lf

*.cat binary
*.cer binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
*.pfx binary
